tr.td:
In adolescents, clinicians should take a careful history and consider the following symptoms as suggestive of the presence of endometriosis:
chronic or acyclical pelvic pain, particularly combined with nausea, dysmenorrhoea, dyschezia, dysuria, dyspareunia;
cyclical pelvic pain (Greene et al., 2009; Treloar et al., 2010; Vicino et al., 2010; Yang et al., 2012; DiVasta et al., 2018).
